---
source: crates/biome_js_analyze/tests/spec_tests.rs
expression: invalid.js
---
# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
if (a < b < c) {}
if (a > b > c) {}
if (a <= b >= c) {}
if (a >= b < c) {}
if (a == b == c) {}
if (a === b === c) {}
if (a != b !== c) {}
if (a !== b == c) {}

// Parentheses don't change the result, and the formatter adds them to equality chains.
if ((a == b) == c) {}
if ((a < b) < c) {}

// One diagnostic for the whole chain.
if (a == b == c == d) {}
if ((a == b == c) == d) {}
if (a < b < c < d) {}

// The right side is not clearly a boolean.
if (a === b === foo()) {}
if (a === b === c.d) {}
const x = a < b < 10;

// Comparing booleans with `<` or `>` is still reported.
if ((a < b) < (c < d)) {}
if (a < b < !c) {}
if (a < b < true) {}

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.js:2:5 lint/nursery/noChainedComparison ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × This compares the result of another comparison with a value.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ if (a < b < c) {}
      │     ^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ if (a > b > c) {}
    4 │ if (a <= b >= c) {}
  
  i This comparison runs first and produces true or false.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ if (a < b < c) {}
      │     ^^^^^
    3 │ if (a > b > c) {}
    4 │ if (a <= b >= c) {}
  
  i This value is then compared with that true or false, not with the values of the first comparison.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ if (a < b < c) {}
      │             ^
    3 │ if (a > b > c) {}
    4 │ if (a <= b >= c) {}
  
  i For example, 3 > 2 > 1 is false, because 3 > 2 is true, and true > 1 is false.
  
  i To compare each pair of values, join separate comparisons with &&, as in a < b && b < c.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

